.TH MKWEBALBUM 1 "2026-08-02" "mkwebalbum 1.4.0"
.SH NAME
mkwebalbum \- generate an HTML photo album from a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkwebalbum
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIinputdir\fR] [\fIoutputfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkwebalbum
generates a responsive HTML page that links to the entries in a directory.
Image files receive thumbnail previews in an adjacent
.I .preview
directory.

Only the top-level directory is processed. By default, only image files are
included, and dot files and directories are ignored. When \fIinputdir\fR is
omitted, the current directory is used.

The output defaults to
.I index.html
in the current directory. Specify
.B -
as \fIoutputfile\fR to write the HTML to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -a
Include all top-level files and directories, rather than image files only.
.TP
.BI -e " regex"
Exclude entries whose names match \fIregex\fR. The default is
.B ^\(rs.
which excludes dot files and directories.
.TP
.B -h
Show usage help.
.TP
.B -r
Regenerate image previews even when they already exist.
.TP
.BI -t " title"
Set the HTML document title. The default is the name of \fIinputdir\fR.
.TP
.B -v
Show the command name and version.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B awk
Formats file sizes in the generated HTML.
.TP
.B ImageMagick
The
.B convert
command generates image previews.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .preview/
Created within the input directory to contain image previews. The directory
also contains an
.I .htaccess
file that disables Apache directory listing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate an album for the current directory:
.nf
.B mkwebalbum
.fi
.TP
Generate an album from a directory with a custom title:
.nf
.B mkwebalbum -t "Summer trip" photos album.html
.fi
.TP
Write an album to standard output:
.nf
.B mkwebalbum photos -
.fi
